     "result_text_tail": "e roadmap slide.\n\n**Choices I made for you:**\n- Board audience, deciding whether to approve the plan, with the storyline approved as drafted.\n- Assumptions, each stated on the slide that uses it:\n  - The four store groups have similar sales.\n  - The best-staffed quarter of stores carries about a quarter of labor cost.\n  - Promotional events are of similar size.\n  - No market growth.\n  - Online sales lost under the new delivery pricing are lost to Harlow entirely.\n- I rounded four stored values slightly (87%, \u22126%, $7.0M, $3.0M) so slide numbers match their titles; this is within the QA tolerance.\n- The pack has no web sources, so the step that re-checks web links didn't apply.\n\n**One QA warning I left on purpose:** on the roadmap slide (page 21), the sidebar gives each move's FY2028 gain, and the check flags these numbers because the timeline itself has none. I kept them because they size each row of the roadmap.\n\nI couldn't view the slides as images here, because no converter is available. I checked them through the layout warnings and a dump of every slide's text instead, so it's worth a quick look in PowerPoint.\n\nNext, I could size the price and vendor-funding offsets to close the wage-rise gap, or switch the theme.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- harlow-margin-plan.pptx\n- harlow-margin-plan-sources.xlsx \u2014 one sheet per slide, plus Calculations with live formulas\n- harlow-margin-plan.json \u2014 the spec, for re-rendering; the script that builds it is in `./work/build_spec.py`"
